Exercise(id:"extended-c1-t3-assignment",topic:"python-c1-t3",category:"Homework",type:"code",title:"Boundary values and decision tables — independent task",prompt:"Define solve(weight) returning Light when weight is below 10, Standard when it is from 10 through 20, and Heavy when it is above 20.\n\nRecord any requested explanation in My Notes.",tests:[{"input": [], "harness": "print(solve(9))", "expected": "Light"}, {"input": [], "harness": "print(solve(10))", "expected": "Standard"}, {"input": [], "harness": "print(solve(20))", "expected": "Standard"}, {"input": [], "harness": "print(solve(21))", "expected": "Heavy"}],hints:["Write down the input, required result, and one small example.", "Try a boundary or empty case allowed by the question. Which part of your reasoning needs adjustment?"],solution:"def solve(weight):\n    if weight < 10:\n        return \"Light\"\n    if weight <= 20:\n        return \"Standard\"\n    return \"Heavy\"",required:false),
