Exercise(id:"extended-c1-t4-assignment",topic:"python-c1-t4",category:"Homework",type:"code",title:"Nested conditions — independent task",prompt:"Define solve(member, credit) returning Join first for a non-member, Add credit for a member with credit at most zero, and Ready otherwise.\n\nRecord any requested explanation in My Notes.",tests:[{"input": [], "harness": "print(solve(False, 5))", "expected": "Join first"}, {"input": [], "harness": "print(solve(True, 0))", "expected": "Add credit"}, {"input": [], "harness": "print(solve(True, 2))", "expected": "Ready"}],hints:["Write down the input, required result, and one small example.", "Try a boundary or empty case allowed by the question. Which part of your reasoning needs adjustment?"],solution:"def solve(member, credit):\n    if not member:\n        return \"Join first\"\n    return \"Ready\" if credit > 0 else \"Add credit\"",required:false),
