Exercise(id:"extended-c2-t0-assignment",topic:"python-c2-t0",category:"Homework",type:"code",title:"while loops and termination — independent task",prompt:"Define solve(n) returning the sum of the integers from 1 through n. n is a nonnegative integer. Use a while loop.\n\nRecord any requested explanation in My Notes.",tests:[{"input": [], "harness": "print(solve(0))", "expected": "0", "comparison": "numeric", "tolerance": 1e-06}, {"input": [], "harness": "print(solve(3))", "expected": "6", "comparison": "numeric", "tolerance": 1e-06}, {"input": [], "harness": "print(solve(5))", "expected": "15", "comparison": "numeric", "tolerance": 1e-06}],hints:["Write down the input, required result, and one small example.", "Try a boundary or empty case allowed by the question. Which part of your reasoning needs adjustment?"],solution:"def solve(n):\n    total = 0\n    while n > 0:\n        total += n\n        n -= 1\n    return total",required:false),
