Exercise(id:"extended-c6-t0-assignment",topic:"python-c6-t0",category:"Homework",type:"code",title:"Opening, reading and closing a text file — independent task",prompt:"Define solve(text) writing text to note.txt and returning the contents read back from that file.\n\nRecord any requested explanation in My Notes.",tests:[{"input": [], "harness": "print(solve('Hello'))", "expected": "Hello"}, {"input": [], "harness": "print(solve('Two words'))", "expected": "Two words"}],hints:["Write down the input, required result, and one small example.", "Try a boundary or empty case allowed by the question. Which part of your reasoning needs adjustment?"],solution:"def solve(text):\n    with open(\"note.txt\", \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as file:\n        file.write(text)\n    with open(\"note.txt\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as file:\n        return file.read()",required:false),
