Exercise(id:"extended-c6-t1-assignment",topic:"python-c6-t1",category:"Homework",type:"code",title:"Writing structured records — independent task",prompt:"Define solve(text) parsing a JSON object and returning its minutes value. Input is valid JSON and contains that field.\n\nRecord any requested explanation in My Notes.",tests:[{"input": [], "harness": "print(solve('{\"minutes\":30}'))", "expected": "30", "comparison": "numeric", "tolerance": 1e-06}, {"input": [], "harness": "print(solve('{\"minutes\":0}'))", "expected": "0", "comparison": "numeric", "tolerance": 1e-06}],hints:["Write down the input, required result, and one small example.", "Try a boundary or empty case allowed by the question. Which part of your reasoning needs adjustment?"],solution:"def solve(text):\n    import json\n    return json.loads(text)[\"minutes\"]",required:false),
