Exercise(id:"extended-c6-t2-assignment",topic:"python-c6-t2",category:"Homework",type:"code",title:"Validating loaded data — independent task",prompt:"Define solve(record) returning True only for a dictionary whose minutes field is a nonnegative integer. Boolean values must not count as integers here.\n\nRecord any requested explanation in My Notes.",tests:[{"input": [], "harness": "print(solve({'minutes': 30}))", "expected": "True"}, {"input": [], "harness": "print(solve({'minutes': True}))", "expected": "False"}, {"input": [], "harness": "print(solve({}))", "expected": "False"}, {"input": [], "harness": "print(solve({'minutes': -1}))", "expected": "False"}],hints:["Write down the input, required result, and one small example.", "Try a boundary or empty case allowed by the question. Which part of your reasoning needs adjustment?"],solution:"def solve(record):\n    return isinstance(record, dict) and type(record.get(\"minutes\")) is int and record[\"minutes\"] >= 0",required:false),
