Exercise(id:"extended-c7-t0-assignment",topic:"python-c7-t0",category:"Homework",type:"code",title:"Matching a simple text pattern — independent task",prompt:"Define solve(text) returning True only when text contains one or more ASCII digits and no other characters.\n\nRecord any requested explanation in My Notes.",tests:[{"input": [], "harness": "print(solve('123'))", "expected": "True"}, {"input": [], "harness": "print(solve('12x'))", "expected": "False"}, {"input": [], "harness": "print(solve(''))", "expected": "False"}],hints:["Write down the input, required result, and one small example.", "Try a boundary or empty case allowed by the question. Which part of your reasoning needs adjustment?"],solution:"def solve(text):\n    import re\n    return re.fullmatch(r\"[0-9]+\", text) is not None",required:false),
