Exercise(id:"extended-c7-t1-assignment",topic:"python-c7-t1",category:"Homework",type:"code",title:"Searching and extracting a group — independent task",prompt:"Define solve(text) returning the integer following minutes= at the first matching position, or None when absent.\n\nRecord any requested explanation in My Notes.",tests:[{"input": [], "harness": "print(solve('minutes=30'))", "expected": "30", "comparison": "numeric", "tolerance": 1e-06}, {"input": [], "harness": "print(solve('x minutes=7 y'))", "expected": "7", "comparison": "numeric", "tolerance": 1e-06}, {"input": [], "harness": "print(solve('none'))", "expected": "None"}],hints:["Write down the input, required result, and one small example.", "Try a boundary or empty case allowed by the question. Which part of your reasoning needs adjustment?"],solution:"def solve(text):\n    import re\n    match = re.search(r\"minutes=([0-9]+)\", text)\n    return int(match.group(1)) if match else None",required:false),
