Exercise(id:"extended-c7-t2-assignment",topic:"python-c7-t2",category:"Homework",type:"code",title:"Testing a pattern against edge cases — independent task",prompt:"Define solve(text) returning True only for two uppercase ASCII letters followed by exactly three ASCII digits.\n\nRecord any requested explanation in My Notes.",tests:[{"input": [], "harness": "print(solve('AB123'))", "expected": "True"}, {"input": [], "harness": "print(solve('A123'))", "expected": "False"}, {"input": [], "harness": "print(solve('AB1234'))", "expected": "False"}, {"input": [], "harness": "print(solve('ab123'))", "expected": "False"}],hints:["Write down the input, required result, and one small example.", "Try a boundary or empty case allowed by the question. Which part of your reasoning needs adjustment?"],solution:"def solve(text):\n    import re\n    return re.fullmatch(r\"[A-Z]{2}[0-9]{3}\", text) is not None",required:false),
