Exercise(id:"extended-c8-t0-assignment",topic:"python-c8-t0",category:"Homework",type:"code",title:"Defining a class and creating objects — independent task",prompt:"Define solve(name) returning Hello, NAME by creating an object with a greeting method.\n\nRecord any requested explanation in My Notes.",tests:[{"input": [], "harness": "print(solve('Amina'))", "expected": "Hello, Amina"}, {"input": [], "harness": "print(solve('Musa'))", "expected": "Hello, Musa"}],hints:["Write down the input, required result, and one small example.", "Try a boundary or empty case allowed by the question. Which part of your reasoning needs adjustment?"],solution:"def solve(name):\n    class Person:\n        def __init__(self, name): self.name = name\n        def greet(self): return f\"Hello, {self.name}\"\n    return Person(name).greet()",required:false),
