Exercise(id:"extended-c8-t2-assignment",topic:"python-c8-t2",category:"Homework",type:"code",title:"Designing a small object interface — independent task",prompt:"Define solve(values) using a counter object to add nonnegative values and returning the final value. Inputs are valid.\n\nRecord any requested explanation in My Notes.",tests:[{"input": [], "harness": "print(solve([2, 3]))", "expected": "5", "comparison": "numeric", "tolerance": 1e-06}, {"input": [], "harness": "print(solve([]))", "expected": "0", "comparison": "numeric", "tolerance": 1e-06}],hints:["Write down the input, required result, and one small example.", "Try a boundary or empty case allowed by the question. Which part of your reasoning needs adjustment?"],solution:"def solve(values):\n    class Counter:\n        def __init__(self): self.value = 0\n        def add(self, amount): self.value += amount\n    counter = Counter()\n    for value in values: counter.add(value)\n    return counter.value",required:false),
